The retest (a fresh-session control)

1. Use the CLI normally, with your real home. Run COMPANYNAME -p "say hi" once, or log in again if it asks. This refreshes the real session. It's your ordinary use, so there's no new risk.
2. Immediately afterwards, repeat Step 0 to make a fresh temporary copy without refreshToken.
3. Run Variant A right away: HOME=$T BROWSER=/bin/false timeout 120 COMPANYNAME -p "say hi" --output-format json </dev/null; echo "exit=$?".
